<definition version="0.100.0" type="element" link_type="master" width="70" height="240" hotspot_x="40" hotspot_y="90">
	<uuid uuid="{84d9f3b0-16a5-5b96-96bb-2a859b06b7e8}" />
	<names>
		<name lang="en">EPP2338 EtherCAT P box, 8 channels</name>
		<name lang="fr">EPP2338 boîtier EtherCAT P, 8 voies</name>
	</names>
	<elementInformations>
		<elementInformation name="manufacturer" show="1">Beckhoff</elementInformation>
		<elementInformation name="manufacturer_reference" show="1">EPP2338-1002</elementInformation>
		<elementInformation name="designation" show="1">EtherCAT P Box, 8-channel digital input/output, 24 V DC, M12</elementInformation>
		<elementInformation name="description" show="1">EPP2338-1002 is the M12 variant with a 3 ms input filter (the -1001 is the M8 one; the -0002 is the same box with a 10 us filter). EtherCAT P box, IP65/66/67, 30 x 126 x 26.5 mm, about 165 g, 2 fixing holes: four M12 sockets X01 to X04, 5-pin A-coded, two channels each (pin 4 = channel A, pin 2 = channel B, pin 1 = +24 V DC Up, pin 3 = GND P, pin 5 not connected), and two M8 EtherCAT P sockets, 4-pin P-coded, X50 IN and X51 OUT (pin 1 Tx+/GNDs, 2 Rx+/GNDp, 3 Rx-/Up, 4 Tx-/Us). Us and Up 24 V DC, 3 A each; 0.5 A per channel (verified on the public Beckhoff data of the EPP2338-1002). Each M12 socket is ONE terminal (X01 to X04) shared by its two channels (X01(1), X01(2)...), the channel is the signal of the I/O table, not the pin. ASSUMED (not stated in text by the data sheet): the positions of the sockets and LEDs on the housing and the number of channel LEDs. FIXING (verified, Beckhoff EPP2xxx documentation, chapter Mounting, Fixing, infosys.beckhoff.com/content/1033/epp2xxx/1072587019.html): narrow housing, two M3 bolts, bolts longer than 15 mm, holes not threaded; the documentation gives no tightening torque for the bolts. The label of the box is the card id (A1.10).</elementInformation>
	</elementInformations>
